# The full gate, and the only one: build, lint, both spec lints, format check, the contract-bundle
# and cross-repo contract checks, then unit, cross-cutting, integration and contract tests.
#
# About 90 seconds, which is why it is not split into tiers. Integration and contract cost 14s and
# 49s against an in-memory Mongo — there is nothing worth trading away, and one gate is easier to
# trust than three.
#
# `check:spec-identity` SKIPS rather than fails when the paired frontend is not on disk, so a
# half-cloned pair can still commit. It stays fatal under CI, where a missing sibling means the
# workflow is misconfigured.
#
# Deliberately not here, and run by hand for the occasions that want them: `test:mutation`
# (re-executes the unit suite once per mutant — nightly in CI), `complete:manual` (`test:prism`,
# which binds a real port), `bench` / `bench:search` (need a running server, and report numbers
# rather than a verdict), and `test:fuzz` — which is nightly until the 500 it found is fixed, see
# docs/theory/known-gaps.md §9.
npm run complete
